STDOUT:
I've written the review to `kibitz-runs/2026-10-23-codex-mobile-map-ideas/r1/claude.md`. The tool check passed, and every claim is tied to a file and line in the repo or marked "verify". I made no other changes.

**Verdict: yes-with-fixes.** The pinch half matches the real code and can be built. The music half needs rework before a slice is chosen.

The main findings:
- **Live site:** `.github/workflows/deploy-pages.yml` deploys the Godot export to the site root on every push to `main`, and `public/` only goes to `/browser`. The only thing stopping a deploy is the `[skip ci]` commit suffix. So any mobile fix that ships takes all of `main` with it. Three places still say otherwise: `godot/project.godot:1`, `session_handoff.md:13` and `session_handoff.md:21`.
- **No phone test route:** the creator's phone only loads the deployed site, and deploying is forbidden. Phone confirmation therefore stays open until the creator approves some way to get a build onto the phone.
- **Music hypotheses:** the plan names only one cause (the audio buffer starving on a single-threaded web build). The code supports a second: a new player hears only sine bass at about 98–147 Hz (`main.gd:10655`, `main.gd:10952`), which phone speakers may barely reproduce. That part is my assumption and needs checking on a device. A third is the phone's OS mute or audio-unlock state, which is unknown.
- **Music test could falsely pass:** a desktop Chromium test that only measures output volume would pass even if the phone stays silent. The review suggests adding a frequency check and a throttled-CPU run, using the existing audio probe in `tests/godot-browser.mjs:141-175` rather than building a new one.
- **Pinch behaviour is undecided:**
  - The existing zoom keeps the camera following the player, while panning stops it. On the phone layout, the follow camera recentres on the player, which would undo a pinch anchored between the fingers.
  - The plan doesn't say whether moving two fingers also pans the map.
  - The rhythm circle (`godot/rhythm_circle.gd:478-493`) handles touch itself and would react to a second finger at the same time.
- **Already in place:** "Zoom +/-" buttons are always on screen, so this is a missing gesture rather than missing zoom. The in-game hint text (`main.gd:14742`) only describes mouse controls, even on phones.

I recommend cutting the slice to pinch plus a touch-aware version of that hint line, with music reduced to diagnosis only and no code change.

Several connectors (GitHub, Slack, Linear, Asana, Atlassian, Datadog, Notion, PagerDuty, Box, Runway) need authorizing before they can be used. Claude.ai connectors are authorized in your claude.ai connector settings; the others via `claude mcp` or `/mcp` in an interactive session. None were needed for this review.
